    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **259 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant and a `countOwnersInCity(city)` helper that counts existing owners in the city case-insensitively (consistent with the existing `nextCustomerCode` city matching).\n- In `addOwner`, after field normalization/validation, the request is rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners. Since the count excludes the not-yet-persisted owner, a city with exactly 50 is full and the 51st is rejected.\n\n**Tests** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`):\n- `createOwnerRejectedWhenCityAtCapacity` \u2014 seeds 50 owners in a unique city, expects the next POST to return 409.\n- `createOwnerAllowedWhenCityBelowCapacity` \u2014 seeds 49 owners, expects the next POST to succeed (201), guarding against an off-by-one.\n\nThe rule only applies to V1's create endpoint; V2 has no `addOwner`, and existing tests use \"Madison\" (4 seeded owners), well under the threshold, so nothing else was affected.",
